			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.29.2020::9:12:1</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset2 Symbol;}}%0D
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue255;}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\b\fs24 Overview:\cf0\b0\fs20\par%0D
This is a CSV Importer for importing simple requirements. The CSV should have three columns - it does not matter what the columns are called as long as they are in this order:\par%0D
\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li360 ID\par%0D
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Name\par%0D
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Specification\par%0D
\pard\par%0D
The importer ignores the first row in the sheet, considering that to be a title row.\par%0D
\par%0D
\cf1\b\fs24 To use:\cf0\b0\fs20\par%0D
Right-click this Requirements Importer and select \b CSV Import Settings\par%0D
\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li360\b0 Set the Import data To field to a Package in the model\par%0D
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Select a CSV file to import\par%0D
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Click Import\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
